  "Helsinki, Finland, Finland": {
    "ratio": [
      {
        "summary": "Helsinki declared itself a “Fair Trade city” in 2013 and has been using fair-trade-related criteria in its procurement. In March 2026, the City Council voted to halve its procurement of meat and dairy products by 2030 and replace it with plant-based food options in schools, hospitals and municipal institutions. There has already been some progress: since 2019, the amount of red meat served has already been cut by half. From 2029, meat dishes will be served only once or twice a week.",
